  "english-meanings-of-the-quran": {
    "description": "This text provides an English translation and theological commentary on selected portions of the Quran, specifically focusing on Sura Al-Fatihah and the opening verses of Sura Al-Baqarah. The author, Rashad Khalifa, presents his work as the first English rendering of the Quranic meanings by a Muslim Arab, intended to clarify fundamental Islamic principles for a contemporary audience. He argues that the Quran possesses a unique linguistic efficiency and a mathematical structure that serves as evidence of its divine origin. Through a combination of verse-by-verse translation and analytical commentary, he explores themes such as the nature of God, the necessity of belief in the hereafter, and the importance of daily prayer. The author further incorporates findings from computerized studies of the text, claiming that the frequency of specific letters and the arrangement of suras demonstrate a divinely ordained system that transcends human capability.",
